WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Support us and become VIP member 
to remove all ads from www.OpenSubtitles.org

2
00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:43.538
Helaena.

3
00:02:45.499 --> 00:02:46.875
Helaena.

4
00:02:48.627 --> 00:02:49.627
Helaena.

5
00:02:57.886 --> 00:02:59.554
I'm sorry to disturb your rest.

6
00:03:00.138 --> 00:03:02.575
Have you heard word from my mother?

7
00:03:02.599 --> 00:03:03.599
No.

8
00:03:04.059 --> 00:03:06.061
Nor do I expect to. until...

9
00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:21.618
Did Aemond ask you
to ride into battle with him?

10
00:03:26.665 --> 00:03:28.250
Lord Corlys imagined he would.

11
00:03:31.712 --> 00:03:33.964
When I was a girl. I wanted to fly.

12
00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:37.134
But now. when...

13
00:03:38.468 --> 00:03:40.011
when I'm with Dreamfyre...

14
00:03:44.349 --> 00:03:45.434
it's...

15
00:03:47.144 --> 00:03:48.937
and then too much.

16
00:03:53.525 --> 00:03:57.088
I think our father felt the same way.

17
00:03:57.112 --> 00:04:00.591
He renounced the strength of dragons
and embraced a quieter life.

18
00:04:00.615 --> 00:04:02.451
He did not wish to be changed.

19
00:04:03.702 --> 00:04:07.873
You believe the dragons
alter us in some way?

20
00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.835
You now have many dragons.

21
00:04:12.878 --> 00:04:15.297
Are you yourself not altered?

22
00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:17.591
No.

23
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.595
Well. I do not wish to be.

24
00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:26.909
I wished only to put an end to our contest

25
00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:29.186
and restore us to our proper order.

26
00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:33.273
Helaena.

27
00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:38.403
Sister. I believe that you...

28
00:04:39.613 --> 00:04:42.157
may be a dreamer.

29
00:04:43.366 --> 00:04:44.576
That you...

30
00:04:45.869 --> 00:04:47.204
see things.

31
00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:52.751
I see flashes sometimes.

32
00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.837
Some clearer than others.

33
00:04:57.672 --> 00:04:59.216
What did you see last?

34
00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:03.470
A gray mare.

35
00:05:09.893 --> 00:05:12.020
What of Daemon? Have you seen him?

36
00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.652
The Winter Wolves. then.

37
00:05:19.653 --> 00:05:21.363
Or Tumbleton.

38
00:05:22.906 --> 00:05:25.468
Will Ormund Hightower be brought to heel?

39
00:05:25.492 --> 00:05:27.053
I don't know.

40
00:05:27.077 --> 00:05:29.663
You don't know? Or you will not say?

41
00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:38.731
You may refuse me as your sister.

42
00:05:38.755 --> 00:05:40.441
but I may compel you as your queen.

43
00:05:40.465 --> 00:05:42.843
Now. tell me what you know!

44
00:05:44.052 --> 00:05:47.990
Tell me there has been no mistake.
that I will prevail.

45
00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:50.141
as the gods must surely intend. Tell me.

46
00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:34.686
Mother.

47
00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:39.024
I told you I would come. if I could.

48
00:06:41.276 --> 00:06:44.195
Were you not taken captive?

49
00:06:46.448 --> 00:06:47.824
Your sister was taken.

50
00:06:49.618 --> 00:06:51.620
But I managed to stay hidden. to escape.

51
00:06:53.914 --> 00:06:56.708
You have been so clever
to remain here undiscovered.

52
00:06:58.168 --> 00:06:59.794
I thought all had forsaken me.

53
00:07:11.473 --> 00:07:13.099
How could I forsake...

54
00:07:13.892 --> 00:07:15.060
my best...

55
00:07:16.603 --> 00:07:18.063
and truest son?

56
00:07:20.565 --> 00:07:22.484
The city has fallen. Aemond.

57
00:07:24.527 --> 00:07:26.571
You're all I have left.

58
00:07:39.542 --> 00:07:43.421
The road has been long and perilous.
so I'll be glad of a bed.

59
00:07:45.799 --> 00:07:47.550
What of Aegon?

60
00:07:49.427 --> 00:07:52.347
Aegon is most likely dead.

61
00:07:55.517 --> 00:07:57.102
I did all I could.

62
00:08:04.067 --> 00:08:05.443
And for you.

63
00:08:12.492 --> 00:08:14.345
But I have failed you. Aemond.

64
00:08:14.369 --> 00:08:15.370
No.

65
00:08:17.205 --> 00:08:19.266
- I was too young.
- Never.

66
00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:20.875
I was just a child.

67
00:09:08.214 --> 00:09:11.801
And in this moment. I will give you a son.

68
00:09:14.262 --> 00:09:15.638
Aemond.

69
00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:23.396
Aemond.

70
00:09:24.606 --> 00:09:26.608
- What have you seen?
- Please.

71
00:09:49.798 --> 00:09:51.216
Aemond.

72
00:10:23.331 --> 00:10:24.833
Open the gates!

73
00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:47.123
They've crossed the Blackwater Rush.

74
00:10:47.147 --> 00:10:49.291
- How many?
- Twenty thousand.

75
00:10:49.315 --> 00:10:50.942
A day's march away. Two at most.

76
00:10:52.902 --> 00:10:57.574
So. your dim but ambitious Dornish friend
died in the mud for nothing.

77
00:10:58.616 --> 00:10:59.760
That is no matter.

78
00:10:59.784 --> 00:11:03.121
I have a piece on the board now
that will bring the bitch to her knees.

79
00:11:05.915 --> 00:11:07.458
And what is that?

80
00:11:44.704 --> 00:11:46.122
- My prince...
- Move!

81
00:11:49.459 --> 00:11:51.628
Where is she? Where's Rhaena?

82
00:11:52.587 --> 00:11:54.857
I see we are dispensing with courtesies.

83
00:11:54.881 --> 00:11:56.382
Is she here?

84
00:11:57.508 --> 00:12:01.572
She flew. just after I sent to you.

85
00:12:01.596 --> 00:12:03.199
I could not hold her.

86
00:12:03.223 --> 00:12:05.850
Put her in chains if you have to.
lock her in a cell.

87
00:12:07.143 --> 00:12:08.954
Do you imagine it's so easy
to force a dragon rider

88
00:12:08.978 --> 00:12:10.730
to do what she does not wish?

89
00:12:12.065 --> 00:12:13.334
She exposes me. too.

90
00:12:13.358 --> 00:12:15.336
She beseeched me with tears in her eyes.

91
00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:17.237
swore that she would
remain here in hiding.

92
00:12:18.988 --> 00:12:20.907
Talk of a dragon rider is rife in the Vale.

93
00:12:21.991 --> 00:12:24.595
The villagers gossip
of a wild girl in the mountains

94
00:12:24.619 --> 00:12:26.138
living amongst nettles and sheep.

95
00:12:26.162 --> 00:12:28.265
I am finished with the matter.

96
00:12:28.289 --> 00:12:30.059
It is in my best interest now
to alert the queen

97
00:12:30.083 --> 00:12:31.584
- to her flight.
- No.

98
00:12:32.627 --> 00:12:35.022
You may blunt Rhaenyra's wrath.
but you will not evade it.

99
00:12:35.046 --> 00:12:36.047
Give me a day.

100
00:12:43.721 --> 00:12:45.139
Please.

101
00:12:48.601 --> 00:12:51.813
She has been here and there
seeking news of Vhagar.

102
00:12:53.481 --> 00:12:55.501
There's word of a sighting
near Fairmarket.

103
00:12:55.525 --> 00:12:57.277
so I can only assume...

104
00:13:04.409 --> 00:13:06.369
We are two days behind Aemond at best.

105
00:13:07.370 --> 00:13:10.206
I have long tired
of this endless searching.

106
00:13:11.791 --> 00:13:14.895
I cannot help but think
I'm being punished by Rhaenyra.

107
00:13:14.919 --> 00:13:16.879
or at least sent far from her sight.

108
00:13:18.715 --> 00:13:21.050
She thinks of us
only as tools to be wielded.

109
00:13:22.844 --> 00:13:26.657
I wondered. my lady.
if I might beg you for a kindness.

110
00:13:26.681 --> 00:13:29.868
My father wishes for Alyn and me
to be legitimized

111
00:13:29.892 --> 00:13:31.561
and take the Velaryon name.

112
00:13:32.312 --> 00:13:34.522
The queen is being reluctant.

113
00:13:35.398 --> 00:13:37.233
You know my standing after the Gullet.

114
00:13:38.151 --> 00:13:40.361
I do not think my words
would have much sway with her.

115
00:13:42.238 --> 00:13:43.990
But your father. perhaps.

116
00:13:45.158 --> 00:13:47.952
Why this concern now
with names and titles?

117
00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:50.306
I understand your grievance.

118
00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:52.516
but surely. you have
a better thing in your dragon

119
00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:54.768
than any lordly appellation.

120
00:13:54.792 --> 00:13:57.021
It is only that if
either of us were to marry.

121
00:13:57.045 --> 00:13:58.171
That is...

122
00:13:59.255 --> 00:14:03.217
if either of us gained the favor
of some highborn lady.

123
00:14:05.845 --> 00:14:08.848
He has spoken to you. then. Your brother.

124
00:14:17.523 --> 00:14:19.150
Is it Vhagar?

125
00:14:22.779 --> 00:14:23.780
No.

126
00:14:24.364 --> 00:14:26.884
I did not think us like
to escape the Red Keep.

127
00:14:26.908 --> 00:14:29.535
But Ser Adrian remained
steadfast and resolute.

128
00:14:30.995 --> 00:14:33.307
He led us to a secret gate

129
00:14:33.331 --> 00:14:35.934
and I had enough coin with me for horses.

130
00:14:35.958 --> 00:14:37.770
We tried to remain off the roads.

131
00:14:37.794 --> 00:14:41.857
but the forests have become
impassable in places.

132
00:14:41.881 --> 00:14:43.466
There are wild men in the woods now.

133
00:14:44.384 --> 00:14:46.737
I would not have arrived here
if it wasn't for him.

134
00:14:46.761 --> 00:14:49.615
Rhaenyra took the castle.
but he remained loyal.

135
00:14:49.639 --> 00:14:51.700
He helped me at great risk
to his own person.

136
00:14:51.724 --> 00:14:52.850
He is a gr...

137
00:14:56.896 --> 00:14:58.272
Have I offended you?

138
00:15:03.111 --> 00:15:04.278
No.

139
00:15:10.868 --> 00:15:12.495
You are all I have left.

140
00:15:28.344 --> 00:15:30.239
This is he.

141
00:15:30.263 --> 00:15:32.408
my protector and guide. Ser Adrian.

142
00:15:32.432 --> 00:15:33.766
Your Grace.

143
00:15:49.407 --> 00:15:52.368
Well. it seems I owe you a debt.

144
00:15:55.163 --> 00:15:57.623
I did only as my conscience demanded.

145
00:15:59.792 --> 00:16:02.086
The queen dowager was treated shamefully.

146
00:16:13.431 --> 00:16:14.474
Aemond!

147
00:16:24.442 --> 00:16:26.110
Sorry. Mother.

148
00:16:28.154 --> 00:16:31.491
There are secrets here.
and I can trust no stranger.

149
00:16:32.533 --> 00:16:34.410
There you are.

150
00:16:36.245 --> 00:16:37.955
You're just in time for supper.

151
00:16:44.378 --> 00:16:48.650
The maesters tell me the fat of livestock
is beneficial to the bones.

152
00:16:48.674 --> 00:16:51.570
But I do wonder how something
so slippery in substance

153
00:16:51.594 --> 00:16:53.429
can truly be benign.

154
00:16:55.598 --> 00:16:57.099
Do try the wine. Lord Corlys.

155
00:16:58.184 --> 00:17:01.229
I find it wards off
the fetid air of this place.

156
00:17:06.734 --> 00:17:09.171
What are you about. Hightower?

157
00:17:09.195 --> 00:17:11.781
Is this some kind of final repast?

158
00:17:12.740 --> 00:17:15.260
Pigeon pie before the executioner's block?

159
00:17:15.284 --> 00:17:16.661
On the contrary.

160
00:17:17.703 --> 00:17:20.498
We hope to enjoy the pleasure
of your company for quite some time.

161
00:17:21.165 --> 00:17:24.210
You will be of great assistance to us
in our little endeavor.

162
00:17:25.419 --> 00:17:28.631
As what? A hostage?

163
00:17:29.882 --> 00:17:31.985
Does the savage queen
harbor such a tender heart

164
00:17:32.009 --> 00:17:35.614
that she should cast away her crown
for the sake of her wayward Hand?

165
00:17:35.638 --> 00:17:37.014
I think not.

166
00:17:38.558 --> 00:17:40.661
The Velaryons. however.

167
00:17:40.685 --> 00:17:43.539
with their lord as forfeit.
the men of Driftmark

168
00:17:43.563 --> 00:17:46.625
will think better
of entering King's Landing.

169
00:17:46.649 --> 00:17:50.278
And without them. the city will again
eat of its own disorder.

170
00:17:54.115 --> 00:17:56.134
How will that help

171
00:17:56.158 --> 00:17:58.286
when the Winter Wolves
are clawing at our gates?

172
00:18:05.668 --> 00:18:07.104
Do you know?

173
00:18:07.128 --> 00:18:10.274
More and more I am inclined

174
00:18:10.298 --> 00:18:11.757
to limit my diet...

175
00:18:13.301 --> 00:18:14.719
to the vegetable kingdom.

176
00:18:16.095 --> 00:18:17.972
Just as the people of Naathi do.

177
00:18:18.764 --> 00:18:21.076
If you have finished
with your instruction...

178
00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:22.852
What do you see in them. anyway?

179
00:18:23.853 --> 00:18:25.396
The Targaryen...

180
00:18:26.897 --> 00:18:28.000
element.

181
00:18:28.024 --> 00:18:32.111
You are a traveled man.
you have seen the world's wonders.

182
00:18:33.279 --> 00:18:37.825
Why limit yourself in tedious alliance
to the brutish and the incurious?

183
00:18:41.454 --> 00:18:44.016
Your wife. of course. was of their blood.

184
00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:46.292
That ended all too predictably.

185
00:18:49.128 --> 00:18:51.732
I would think. after having seen

186
00:18:51.756 --> 00:18:53.799
how they devour one of their own...

187
00:18:56.927 --> 00:18:58.638
I would like to return to my cell.

188
00:18:59.847 --> 00:19:01.307
As you please.

189
00:19:05.561 --> 00:19:06.872
Lord Corlys?

190
00:19:06.896 --> 00:19:08.147
Before you go...

191
00:19:09.857 --> 00:19:11.776
He was in uncommon good spirits...

192
00:19:12.902 --> 00:19:15.213
as though he were on the eve
of some great victory.

193
00:19:15.237 --> 00:19:17.591
He seems to believe that
with Lord Corlys as hos...

194
00:19:17.615 --> 00:19:19.367
Is this his "piece on the board"?

195
00:19:21.118 --> 00:19:23.180
What does the order or disorder
of King's Landing

196
00:19:23.204 --> 00:19:25.331
matter to us now
with an army at the gates?

197
00:19:26.082 --> 00:19:27.375
I'm supposed to be the king.

198
00:19:29.585 --> 00:19:31.521
What sort of ruler am I?

199
00:19:31.545 --> 00:19:35.966
Am I to sit by impotent while a madman
offers us up for the slaughter?

200
00:19:37.885 --> 00:19:39.804
And all of our men with us?

201
00:19:41.514 --> 00:19:43.140
Seems there's no escaping it.

202
00:19:44.266 --> 00:19:47.561
The dream some have of covering themselves
in everlasting glory...

203
00:19:49.063 --> 00:19:51.399
of somehow transcending
humanity's common fate.

204
00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:58.656
I am sorry about your friend.

205
00:20:01.951 --> 00:20:04.078
He gave himself to the dust.

206
00:20:10.126 --> 00:20:11.919
I could order the army to surrender.

207
00:20:12.503 --> 00:20:14.064
And then what?

208
00:20:14.088 --> 00:20:15.965
Have us all marched to the gallows?

209
00:20:18.676 --> 00:20:21.595
You could fly away on Tessarion.

210
00:20:22.805 --> 00:20:24.199
Without you as a pretext for...

211
00:20:24.223 --> 00:20:26.183
He would continue as he began.

212
00:20:27.935 --> 00:20:29.955
Where would I go?

213
00:20:29.979 --> 00:20:33.065
Who would receive a king
who left his own men to their ruin?

214
00:20:36.402 --> 00:20:38.738
I have no fear of insignificance. Gwayne.

215
00:20:42.742 --> 00:20:44.952
Rhaenyra may keep her crown.
for all I care.

216
00:20:48.622 --> 00:20:50.642
Frankly. it is outrageous.

217
00:20:50.666 --> 00:20:53.895
There is a campaign against me!
Jeering in the streets.

218
00:20:53.919 --> 00:20:57.190
My own daughter found
the doorstep of my city dwelling

219
00:20:57.214 --> 00:21:00.134
smeared with some sort of foul matter.

220
00:21:01.844 --> 00:21:03.989
I don't know what you
want me to do about it.

221
00:21:04.013 --> 00:21:05.264
My queen.

222
00:21:06.348 --> 00:21:07.348
With respect.

223
00:21:08.601 --> 00:21:11.747
In front of petitioners.
you named me responsible

224
00:21:11.771 --> 00:21:15.125
for the current financial
grievances in the city.

225
00:21:15.149 --> 00:21:16.460
I hardly be...

226
00:21:16.484 --> 00:21:18.164
Well. what have you done
to alleviate them?

227
00:21:18.903 --> 00:21:20.529
What can I do?

228
00:21:21.697 --> 00:21:24.450
I have advocated for a tax.
It has fallen on deaf ears.

229
00:21:25.367 --> 00:21:29.473
Our dribbles of gold are spent
as fast as they are gathered.

230
00:21:29.497 --> 00:21:33.793
It's as if I have been installed here
as some sort of scapegoat.

231
00:21:38.214 --> 00:21:40.090
Has there been any word from Lord Corlys?

232
00:21:41.967 --> 00:21:43.177
From Harrenhal?

233
00:21:46.430 --> 00:21:49.618
- And Daemon?
- Absent.

234
00:21:49.642 --> 00:21:52.204
The prince is on some...

235
00:21:52.228 --> 00:21:53.914
errand of his own.

236
00:21:53.938 --> 00:21:57.542
The Keepers say he flew out
of the city before dawn.

237
00:21:57.566 --> 00:22:01.254
The river host are but a day's march
from Tumbleton. Your Grace.

238
00:22:01.278 --> 00:22:03.840
and the Velaryon forces will be
at King's Landing on the morrow.

239
00:22:03.864 --> 00:22:07.177
I have a reputation to uphold.

240
00:22:07.201 --> 00:22:12.724
If Ser Adrian has been successful
in his endeavor. of course.

241
00:22:12.748 --> 00:22:15.393
then there is the small matter
of Harrenhal...

242
00:22:15.417 --> 00:22:17.753
Just take it.

243
00:22:18.671 --> 00:22:20.273
Your Grace?

244
00:22:20.297 --> 00:22:22.400
Return to the Twins

245
00:22:22.424 --> 00:22:25.761
and lead the men you have
left there to Harrenhal.

246
00:22:27.680 --> 00:22:29.908
This I will do gladly!

247
00:22:29.932 --> 00:22:31.910
If Aemond is dead. all the better.

248
00:22:31.934 --> 00:22:33.703
But in any case.
you shall occupy it again.

249
00:22:33.727 --> 00:22:35.205
and leave no place for him to return.

250
00:22:35.229 --> 00:22:36.480
My queen.

251
00:22:38.941 --> 00:22:40.919
We have seen something strange.

252
00:22:40.943 --> 00:22:42.546
- Vhagar?
- No.

253
00:22:42.570 --> 00:22:44.631
Sheep stealer. In the Riverlands.

254
00:22:44.655 --> 00:22:46.574
on the banks of the Blue Fork
near Fairmarket.

255
00:22:47.575 --> 00:22:49.219
That is unexpected. He's not known...

256
00:22:49.243 --> 00:22:50.953
Your Grace. he has a rider.

257
00:22:52.329 --> 00:22:55.058
- A new rider?
- I could not say.

258
00:22:55.082 --> 00:22:57.293
We gave chase. but lost him in the hills.

259
00:23:02.548 --> 00:23:04.568
That head Daemon brought to you.

260
00:23:04.592 --> 00:23:06.736
can you say in honesty
you've had no doubts?

261
00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:09.739
He was long in the Riverlands.
and now Sheep stealer

262
00:23:09.763 --> 00:23:12.742
is sighted there with a rider
he assured you was dead.

263
00:23:12.766 --> 00:23:14.703
And in that same moment.

264
00:23:14.727 --> 00:23:17.372
he has absented himself
without explanation.

265
00:23:17.396 --> 00:23:19.791
I have known him to lie.
but this is a great...

266
00:23:19.815 --> 00:23:22.752
You and I have known him to be
capable of far worse than lies.

267
00:23:22.776 --> 00:23:27.048
He has chafed since you arrived here
over your restraint in wielding power.

268
00:23:27.072 --> 00:23:29.301
He is impetuous and impatient.

269
00:23:29.325 --> 00:23:31.720
Who can say what alliance
he may have formed in secret

270
00:23:31.744 --> 00:23:34.914
- when he found you lacking.
- He has sworn to serve me.

271
00:23:36.248 --> 00:23:38.602
I cannot believe that now.
when I need him most.

272
00:23:38.626 --> 00:23:40.085
- that he would...
- Forgive me.

273
00:23:45.215 --> 00:23:46.342
Your Grace.

274
00:23:50.012 --> 00:23:54.308
But is there anything Daemon could do
that you would truly not believe?

275
00:23:59.229 --> 00:24:00.773
Fetch Ser Addam.

276
00:24:09.281 --> 00:24:11.468
They say it is the strength
of the sun in Volantis

277
00:24:11.492 --> 00:24:13.369
that makes for such sweetness
in the grape.

278
00:24:14.870 --> 00:24:17.140
If you mean to console me for this folly

279
00:24:17.164 --> 00:24:19.643
with Volantene wines.
you're much mistaken.

280
00:24:19.667 --> 00:24:22.312
Your Grace. I beg you. reconsider.

281
00:24:22.336 --> 00:24:25.315
At Maidenpool. we might take ship
for Casterly Rock instead.

282
00:24:25.339 --> 00:24:27.776
No. I am decided on Braavos.

283
00:24:27.800 --> 00:24:29.861
How much further must we ride?

284
00:24:29.885 --> 00:24:31.303
Some days still to the port.

285
00:24:32.388 --> 00:24:34.491
Braavos will prove itself
a most cultivated city.

286
00:24:34.515 --> 00:24:35.849
I assure you.

287
00:24:36.475 --> 00:24:37.977
Perhaps even a home from home.

288
00:24:42.856 --> 00:24:43.856
Whoa.

289
00:24:44.525 --> 00:24:47.295
My good woman. what is it you flee?

290
00:24:47.319 --> 00:24:48.964
An army marches this way.

291
00:24:48.988 --> 00:24:51.257
- Some thousand strong.
- Which army?

292
00:24:51.281 --> 00:24:53.843
My daughter said she saw
the red fish on the white.

293
00:24:53.867 --> 00:24:56.429
- The Mootons.
- That's where we are going. to Maidenpool.

294
00:24:56.453 --> 00:24:59.099
We must keep moving.
Turn back if you can.

295
00:24:59.123 --> 00:25:00.624
Mootons are sworn to Rhaenyra.

296
00:25:02.084 --> 00:25:03.711
They can't have heard about me?

297
00:25:16.932 --> 00:25:18.434
The road is lost to us.

298
00:25:19.435 --> 00:25:21.955
We must fall back to Rook's Rest.

299
00:25:21.979 --> 00:25:24.416
We can't go back there.
We may have been discovered.

300
00:25:24.440 --> 00:25:27.317
There is an army coming for us
and we have no place to shelter.

301
00:25:28.736 --> 00:25:31.673
There are thick walls at Rook's Rest
and enough men to defend them.

302
00:25:31.697 --> 00:25:34.783
It shall be refuge for His Grace
till Mooton's host has passed.

303
00:25:40.497 --> 00:25:41.665
You must be famished.

304
00:25:43.083 --> 00:25:45.044
It's a long journey from King's Landing.

305
00:25:47.463 --> 00:25:48.464
Yes.

306
00:25:50.507 --> 00:25:51.800
And fraught. no doubt.

307
00:25:53.343 --> 00:25:55.783
If half the tales I have heard
about the King's Road are true.

308
00:25:59.016 --> 00:26:01.286
How is it that the two of you

309
00:26:01.310 --> 00:26:02.811
came to know one another?

310
00:26:06.940 --> 00:26:08.358
She saved my life.

311
00:26:10.486 --> 00:26:12.130
At whose behest?

312
00:26:12.154 --> 00:26:13.363
Your lord's?

313
00:26:13.989 --> 00:26:15.824
I generally follow my own dictates.

314
00:26:18.494 --> 00:26:21.163
Aemond. I still don't understand
who this woman is.

315
00:26:25.542 --> 00:26:27.544
She is a lady.

316
00:26:29.088 --> 00:26:30.881
And a maester. of sorts.

317
00:26:33.092 --> 00:26:35.928
The care of the castle
has fallen to her for now.

318
00:26:38.347 --> 00:26:43.352
I've decided to stay here with her
and make this place my seat.

319
00:26:45.979 --> 00:26:47.749
Your seat?

320
00:26:47.773 --> 00:26:49.775
Was that not what you yourself suggested?

321
00:26:51.026 --> 00:26:52.796
A new fortress from which to rule.

322
00:26:52.820 --> 00:26:56.674
Rhaenyra has the throne
and six dragons to her name.

323
00:26:56.698 --> 00:26:59.867
It is she who rules now. as much as we
might wish it otherwise.

324
00:27:01.120 --> 00:27:04.832
Rhaenyra's dragons
are ridden by commoners.

325
00:27:06.500 --> 00:27:10.396
She's defiled our great house.
diminished the Iron Throne.

326
00:27:10.420 --> 00:27:12.422
and sowed the seeds of her own ruin.

327
00:27:14.049 --> 00:27:15.551
She will certainly fail.

328
00:27:18.137 --> 00:27:20.806
And we will raise our own throne.

329
00:27:22.516 --> 00:27:25.477
In the mud of the Riverlands.

330
00:27:27.688 --> 00:27:29.189
A new dawn is coming.

331
00:27:32.067 --> 00:27:34.319
A new line of unsullied kings.

332
00:27:37.656 --> 00:27:39.366
We need only to bide our time.

333
00:27:41.743 --> 00:27:43.245
And you. Mother.

334
00:27:45.164 --> 00:27:46.957
You will wait with us.

335
00:27:48.417 --> 00:27:50.645
You have worth yet to offer.

336
00:27:50.669 --> 00:27:53.422
I'm sure your mother will wish to move on.

337
00:27:54.882 --> 00:27:57.318
Back to Oldtown. perhaps.

338
00:27:57.342 --> 00:27:59.445
Our climate doesn't seem to suit her.

339
00:27:59.469 --> 00:28:01.114
There's nothing for her there.

340
00:28:01.138 --> 00:28:02.198
I am all she has left.

341
00:28:02.222 --> 00:28:03.599
- There is Helaena.
- No!

342
00:28:04.516 --> 00:28:06.018
You'll stay with us.

343
00:28:10.898 --> 00:28:12.316
We're out of wood.

344
00:28:20.199 --> 00:28:23.595
I will not be coddled or admonished
like a witless child.

345
00:28:23.619 --> 00:28:25.829
Tread carefully with her. Aemond.

346
00:28:26.914 --> 00:28:28.766
She's come to do you some ill.

347
00:28:28.790 --> 00:28:30.500
She is my blood.

348
00:28:31.668 --> 00:28:33.104
And thus without blemish?

349
00:28:33.128 --> 00:28:36.089
She's always had her secrets.
most of them poorly kept.

350
00:28:37.174 --> 00:28:40.219
My designs for our future
did not include your mother.

351
00:28:40.928 --> 00:28:42.346
And there is the truth of it.

352
00:28:43.305 --> 00:28:44.765
You want me for yourself.

353
00:28:46.934 --> 00:28:48.894
There is a fog that surrounds her.

354
00:28:51.438 --> 00:28:53.899
She has come to do you some evil.

355
00:28:55.525 --> 00:28:58.153
You would be wise to keep
your dark thoughts to yourself.

356
00:29:06.245 --> 00:29:09.248
You Targaryen boys all want
the same thing. don't you?

357
00:30:01.216 --> 00:30:02.467
Tom Tangletongue. what news?

358
00:30:03.468 --> 00:30:07.156
Lord Mooton of Maidenpool.
he's dispatched an army.

359
00:30:07.180 --> 00:30:08.432
They're marching in haste.

360
00:30:09.850 --> 00:30:13.061
Have you not seen our Janos?
I thought he'd be with you.

361
00:30:14.104 --> 00:30:15.707
No. Where are they marching?

362
00:30:15.731 --> 00:30:17.875
They were commanded here. to Rook's Rest.

363
00:30:17.899 --> 00:30:20.753
But they're going
village to village. it seems.

364
00:30:20.777 --> 00:30:22.863
in search of your friend Lannister.

365
00:30:23.989 --> 00:30:26.074
Something about the queen's gold.

366
00:30:26.908 --> 00:30:29.703
They'll be here before we know it.
You'd best be on the move.

367
00:30:41.840 --> 00:30:44.551
I think you'll agree. Ser Tyland.
that you should give yourself up.

368
00:30:45.469 --> 00:30:46.803
She will flay me alive.

369
00:30:47.471 --> 00:30:49.449
No doubt. But once Mooton
has you in hand.

370
00:30:49.473 --> 00:30:51.409
he'll turn towards King's Landing.
and His Grace and I

371
00:30:51.433 --> 00:30:52.660
may yet slip away.

372
00:30:52.684 --> 00:30:54.037
Give the king to me and my men.

373
00:30:54.061 --> 00:30:56.039
We will ride hard
and escape Mooton's clutches.

374
00:30:56.063 --> 00:30:58.041
Must you be so thick?

375
00:30:58.065 --> 00:30:59.709
Rhaenyra is hunting you.

376
00:30:59.733 --> 00:31:01.836
His Grace is not safe in your company.

377
00:31:01.860 --> 00:31:04.088
Turn yourself in
and give him the chance to flee.

378
00:31:04.112 --> 00:31:05.340
Him or you?

379
00:31:05.364 --> 00:31:07.342
It is the honorable thing to do.

380
00:31:07.366 --> 00:31:09.242
- Your Grace. for now. at least...
- No.

381
00:31:11.995 --> 00:31:13.389
No.

382
00:31:13.413 --> 00:31:15.040
Go where you will.

383
00:31:15.999 --> 00:31:17.209
Both of you.

384
00:31:18.251 --> 00:31:19.878
Preserve your own skins.

385
00:31:21.171 --> 00:31:22.732
But I shall run no more.

386
00:31:22.756 --> 00:31:24.817
If you do not run.
Your Grace. you will die.

387
00:31:24.841 --> 00:31:26.152
Then I'll die.

388
00:31:26.176 --> 00:31:27.803
But not as a fugitive.

389
00:31:30.180 --> 00:31:32.307
Unknown. Covered in dust.

390
00:31:33.016 --> 00:31:37.687
Not with an arrow in my back
or trapped like a fox in a hole.

391
00:31:38.939 --> 00:31:41.000
This is absurd. Ser Tyland. I entreat you

392
00:31:41.024 --> 00:31:42.085
to reason with His Grace.

393
00:31:42.109 --> 00:31:43.235
I'll make my stand here.

394
00:31:45.487 --> 00:31:46.780
And be buried as a king.

395
00:31:48.448 --> 00:31:49.866
With my dragon.

396
00:31:53.662 --> 00:31:56.182
I will not have the histories
say that I was slain

397
00:31:56.206 --> 00:31:58.458
in ignominy by my own brother.

398
00:32:04.881 --> 00:32:06.967
If the king wishes to remain. then...

399
00:32:09.177 --> 00:32:10.988
I shall remain with him.

400
00:32:11.012 --> 00:32:13.140
I cannot leave him to face
an army meant for me.

401
00:32:21.481 --> 00:32:23.150
You're resolved in this then?

402
00:32:30.574 --> 00:32:31.908
Well then. my lords...

403
00:32:33.368 --> 00:32:35.912
it seems there is only one thing
left for me to do.

404
00:32:37.497 --> 00:32:39.434
May the Seven be ever at your side.

405
00:32:39.458 --> 00:32:41.436
You would abandon your master?

406
00:32:41.460 --> 00:32:43.795
I am a cripple. Ser Tyland.

407
00:32:45.922 --> 00:32:48.067
Humble enough to admit
that my presence in a fight

408
00:32:48.091 --> 00:32:49.634
would make no earthly difference.

409
00:32:52.679 --> 00:32:55.098
Of course. if my king
commanded me to stay...

410
00:32:57.100 --> 00:32:58.810
What Lord Larys says is true.

411
00:33:00.854 --> 00:33:02.731
He would be no use to us here.

412
00:33:03.899 --> 00:33:05.108
Well. then.

413
00:33:06.860 --> 00:33:10.030
It will be my duty to see
that King Aegon is remembered.

414
00:33:11.990 --> 00:33:15.344
His heroic last hours
immortalized through story...

415
00:33:15.368 --> 00:33:16.995
and song.

416
00:33:21.082 --> 00:33:22.459
Your Grace.

417
00:33:36.473 --> 00:33:37.682
Your Grace.

418
00:33:38.892 --> 00:33:40.185
Come. come. come.

419
00:34:30.860 --> 00:34:32.755
- Stay back!
- You swore to me.

420
00:34:32.779 --> 00:34:34.882
- You should not have come.
- Did you think she would not hear of this?

421
00:34:34.906 --> 00:34:37.701
Stay back! He does not heed me!

422
00:34:42.414 --> 00:34:43.415
<i>Daor!</i>

423
00:34:48.712 --> 00:34:49.963
<i>Daor!</i>

424
00:34:56.845 --> 00:34:59.073
What do you hope to do here?
In the reeds and the mud?

425
00:34:59.097 --> 00:35:00.783
Vhagar was here.

426
00:35:00.807 --> 00:35:02.243
Or near here. last I heard.

427
00:35:02.267 --> 00:35:03.786
We heard the same. but she is gone.

428
00:35:03.810 --> 00:35:05.288
Then I will fly in search of her.

429
00:35:05.312 --> 00:35:06.646
And if you find her?

430
00:35:07.397 --> 00:35:09.625
I thought I could do this. but I can't.

431
00:35:09.649 --> 00:35:12.611
I cannot live the way I have.
cut off from all who loved me.

432
00:35:13.403 --> 00:35:15.780
And so. you think by going
after Vhagar. you will...

433
00:35:17.032 --> 00:35:18.158
what?

434
00:35:18.742 --> 00:35:19.927
If I kill her.

435
00:35:19.951 --> 00:35:21.887
I will have paid
some of my debt to Rhaenyra.

436
00:35:21.911 --> 00:35:24.098
I would at least have grounds
to sue for her mercy.

437
00:35:24.122 --> 00:35:26.225
- You will more likely die.
- Then I will have paid all of it.

438
00:35:26.249 --> 00:35:28.627
I will die absolved
if I cannot live that way.

439
00:35:38.595 --> 00:35:39.763
Let me help you. then.

440
00:35:41.389 --> 00:35:43.016
You cannot battle Vhagar alone.

441
00:35:44.309 --> 00:35:46.061
But the two of us may yet prevail.

442
00:35:47.854 --> 00:35:49.397
Why would you do such a thing?

443
00:35:51.107 --> 00:35:53.777
I had no dragon either when I was young.
Did you know that?

444
00:35:55.153 --> 00:35:57.840
My mother died in child bed
when I was three years of age.

445
00:35:57.864 --> 00:35:59.717
My brother sank into sadness.

446
00:35:59.741 --> 00:36:02.118
I was alone. just as you have been.

447
00:36:05.914 --> 00:36:07.624
I should have done better. Rhaena.

448
00:36:16.007 --> 00:36:18.944
- You lie.
- I did not summon them.

449
00:36:18.968 --> 00:36:22.281
- You'd betray your own daughter?
- I have not. I swear it.

450
00:36:22.305 --> 00:36:23.665
She does not yet know who you are.

451
00:36:25.558 --> 00:36:26.702
Leave him.

452
00:36:26.726 --> 00:36:28.395
They will tear you from the sky.

453
00:36:31.147 --> 00:36:32.774
Run! Run!

454
00:36:47.414 --> 00:36:48.581
Go!

455
00:37:03.805 --> 00:37:05.074
- Call off your dragon!
- What is your agreement

456
00:37:05.098 --> 00:37:06.558
with Sheepstealer's rider?

457
00:37:07.142 --> 00:37:08.202
Answer carefully.

458
00:37:08.226 --> 00:37:10.204
You will not have
another chance to deceive me.

459
00:37:10.228 --> 00:37:11.706
I never wished to deceive you.

460
00:37:11.730 --> 00:37:13.523
- Then. speak!
- Call off your dragon.

461
00:37:21.865 --> 00:37:24.093
Please. Rhaenyra.

462
00:37:24.117 --> 00:37:25.535
She's not herself.

463
00:37:39.758 --> 00:37:40.800
Rhaena?

464
00:37:45.972 --> 00:37:47.348
It wasn't you.

465
00:37:57.692 --> 00:38:00.337
She was Sheepstealer's rider?

466
00:38:00.361 --> 00:38:02.405
All this time. you knew.

467
00:38:07.076 --> 00:38:08.453
This is finished!

468
00:38:20.965 --> 00:38:21.966
Move!

469
00:39:12.392 --> 00:39:15.603
- Your Grace!
- Help Daemon! Go!

470
00:39:16.813 --> 00:39:17.814
Go!

471
00:39:32.662 --> 00:39:33.830
With me!

472
00:39:41.754 --> 00:39:42.755
No!

473
00:39:51.431 --> 00:39:54.309
Escort the queen. I will finish this.

474
00:40:54.285 --> 00:40:57.056
It is magnificent in its way.

475
00:40:57.080 --> 00:41:00.416
I saw it once before
when I petitioned the queen.

476
00:41:04.754 --> 00:41:07.006
Do you know what it brings to my mind?

477
00:41:08.132 --> 00:41:11.678
A hundred sharp little cocks
all vying for attention.

478
00:41:13.304 --> 00:41:17.767
The queen wishes at the moment
to hear no more petitions.

479
00:41:18.726 --> 00:41:20.269
That is a mistake.

480
00:41:21.187 --> 00:41:22.748
I agree.

481
00:41:22.772 --> 00:41:24.941
There is villainy and violence
on her streets now.

482
00:41:26.943 --> 00:41:28.921
The people are afraid to go out by night.

483
00:41:28.945 --> 00:41:30.655
It is to her detriment only.

484
00:41:31.698 --> 00:41:35.868
Those who look to her for relief
now feel she's turned her back on them.

485
00:41:38.746 --> 00:41:42.601
I wished to hear from you
how you fare in this city.

486
00:41:42.625 --> 00:41:45.396
And if there are others
who may find it a consolation

487
00:41:45.420 --> 00:41:49.298
to come to me with their troubles
and have them considered.

488
00:41:50.633 --> 00:41:53.570
You make yourself her proxy.

489
00:41:53.594 --> 00:41:55.572
Someone must. Do you not agree?

490
00:41:55.596 --> 00:41:57.741
If she herself is reluctant.

491
00:41:57.765 --> 00:42:00.911
I can perhaps then bring
certain dilemmas before her

492
00:42:00.935 --> 00:42:04.522
when I judge her mood
to be more accommodating.

493
00:42:07.316 --> 00:42:09.277
You are changed.

494
00:42:12.113 --> 00:42:13.364
This...

495
00:42:13.948 --> 00:42:15.241
has changed you.

496
00:42:16.242 --> 00:42:20.014
My heart is with the downtrodden
as it has ever been.

497
00:42:20.038 --> 00:42:21.122
Is it?

498
00:42:21.748 --> 00:42:25.543
Or have you styled yourself a champion
in order to access these halls?

499
00:42:27.920 --> 00:42:29.005
Look at you.

500
00:42:30.006 --> 00:42:31.442
Standing at the foot of the throne

501
00:42:31.466 --> 00:42:33.777
wearing a silk worth a year
of my earnings.

502
00:42:33.801 --> 00:42:36.137
promising to whisper
into the ear of a queen.

503
00:42:37.472 --> 00:42:40.492
You thrill now to a tune
you once abhorred.

504
00:42:40.516 --> 00:42:43.245
Does it not occur to you
that from this position

505
00:42:43.269 --> 00:42:45.748
I may help those who have no avenue?

506
00:42:45.772 --> 00:42:48.941
What power do you have in truth?

507
00:42:50.443 --> 00:42:52.528
Except to flatter and cajole?

508
00:42:57.784 --> 00:42:59.202
Is that why you called me here?

509
00:43:00.411 --> 00:43:03.331
To look on the trappings so that
someone would hold you in awe?

510
00:43:06.042 --> 00:43:07.627
This was a mistake.

511
00:43:09.087 --> 00:43:11.356
How common I must seem to you.

512
00:43:11.380 --> 00:43:12.673
That will be all.

513
00:43:15.760 --> 00:43:17.845
Some advice. my lady.

514
00:43:19.263 --> 00:43:21.867
These people are not your own.

515
00:43:21.891 --> 00:43:23.684
You would do well to remember that.

516
00:43:25.061 --> 00:43:27.122
Within the walls of the highborn.

517
00:43:27.146 --> 00:43:31.192
a whore will always
and ever remain a whore.

518
00:43:53.756 --> 00:43:54.841
Find her a room.

519
00:43:55.633 --> 00:43:57.051
I do not wish to see her.

520
00:44:03.599 --> 00:44:04.934
Aemond?

521
00:44:08.229 --> 00:44:09.313
Mother.

522
00:44:21.033 --> 00:44:22.553
Your friend Alys.

523
00:44:22.577 --> 00:44:24.328
She's not my friend.

524
00:44:25.705 --> 00:44:27.415
She doesn't want me to stay here.

525
00:44:28.040 --> 00:44:30.769
If I'm disturbing
some understanding between...

526
00:44:30.793 --> 00:44:32.104
No.

527
00:44:32.128 --> 00:44:34.189
- I should perhaps not have come.
- No.

528
00:44:34.213 --> 00:44:37.133
I will take my leave.
if that would behoove you.

529
00:44:38.384 --> 00:44:39.927
I'm glad you came.

530
00:44:43.931 --> 00:44:45.433
I brought you something.

531
00:44:51.272 --> 00:44:52.732
Spiced wine.

532
00:44:54.734 --> 00:44:57.653
I remember a time when you would
not fall asleep without it.

533
00:45:04.243 --> 00:45:05.870
Alys doesn't trust you.

534
00:45:14.837 --> 00:45:16.297
Who do you trust?

535
00:45:20.718 --> 00:45:21.719
I...

536
00:45:23.387 --> 00:45:25.264
I tried to kill Aegon.

537
00:45:35.358 --> 00:45:36.442
I know.

538
00:45:39.362 --> 00:45:40.780
My dear...

539
00:45:42.531 --> 00:45:43.950
foolish boy.

540
00:45:56.128 --> 00:45:57.128
Your Grace.

541
00:46:05.471 --> 00:46:06.681
No. stay.

542
00:46:22.405 --> 00:46:24.198
She implored me not to tell you.

543
00:46:31.163 --> 00:46:33.725
She could not face you.
I wished only to protect her.

544
00:46:33.749 --> 00:46:34.851
From what?

545
00:46:34.875 --> 00:46:36.419
What do you think I am?

546
00:46:38.004 --> 00:46:39.839
You are my wife.

547
00:46:40.423 --> 00:46:43.968
She's my daughter.
One I have long neglected.

548
00:46:47.138 --> 00:46:50.766
Was she not seeking. in all this.
my favor or yours?

549
00:46:52.977 --> 00:46:57.648
I have looked a hundred times
at that skull you brought...

550
00:46:59.358 --> 00:47:02.194
thinking it was the villain
who killed my son.

551
00:47:06.157 --> 00:47:07.884
I am sorry.

552
00:47:07.908 --> 00:47:10.870
but you must see now that
I kept no scheme against you.

553
00:47:13.205 --> 00:47:15.541
I did only what I thought was best.
Rhaenyra.

554
00:47:20.379 --> 00:47:21.547
Please.

555
00:47:25.468 --> 00:47:26.761
It's late.

556
00:48:02.922 --> 00:48:04.340
I am sorry.

557
00:48:06.592 --> 00:48:07.885
To Jace.

558
00:48:10.721 --> 00:48:11.615
To you.

559
00:48:11.639 --> 00:48:13.724
- You would have been queen.
- Enough.

560
00:48:33.661 --> 00:48:35.162
You will begin anew.

561
00:48:43.045 --> 00:48:46.215
More Hightower loyalists were found.
Alert the confessors.

562
00:48:50.886 --> 00:48:51.929
Ser Alyn.

563
00:48:53.305 --> 00:48:54.598
It was left for you.

564
00:49:28.132 --> 00:49:29.133
Alys.

565
00:49:33.679 --> 00:49:34.805
Idiot.

566
00:50:45.459 --> 00:50:47.294
<i>Dracarys!</i>

567
00:51:52.943 --> 00:51:55.863
<i>It was Rhaena he was hiding all along.</i>

568
00:51:58.782 --> 00:52:01.219
He lied. I did not lead you astray.

569
00:52:01.243 --> 00:52:03.972
And yet you cannot say he betrayed me

570
00:52:03.996 --> 00:52:06.391
so much as he would not
betray his daughter.

571
00:52:06.415 --> 00:52:07.809
This time.

572
00:52:07.833 --> 00:52:10.687
But does it not prove
he is willing to deceive you

573
00:52:10.711 --> 00:52:12.546
if he judges it necessary?

574
00:52:13.464 --> 00:52:15.483
And you've never done the same?

575
00:52:15.507 --> 00:52:17.569
I've acted only in your interests.

576
00:52:17.593 --> 00:52:19.762
You have sought to turn me from him.

577
00:52:20.846 --> 00:52:24.784
Pouring your honey in my ear.
whispering. encouraging.

578
00:52:24.808 --> 00:52:27.120
seeking to make me in your image.

579
00:52:27.144 --> 00:52:28.830
In my image?

580
00:52:28.854 --> 00:52:32.042
Your Grace. have I ever
counseled you to do aught

581
00:52:32.066 --> 00:52:35.295
but what Viserys
would have you do in his place?

582
00:52:35.319 --> 00:52:37.964
As you have ofttimes said.
is your own desire.

583
00:52:37.988 --> 00:52:41.325
Yes. and in hewing to his vision.
what have I reaped?

584
00:52:42.284 --> 00:52:44.429
Peace? Prosperity?

585
00:52:44.453 --> 00:52:46.789
The gratitude of my subjects.

586
00:52:54.880 --> 00:52:56.632
My father was not a dreamer.

587
00:52:58.133 --> 00:52:59.968
But his whole life was a dream.

588
00:53:03.555 --> 00:53:05.099
Do not lose faith.

589
00:53:06.934 --> 00:53:09.937
You are on the precipice
of a great victory.

590
00:53:11.980 --> 00:53:15.651
The uncertainties that oppress you
will soon be resolved.

591
00:53:16.652 --> 00:53:20.114
Those who oppose you will fall away.

592
00:53:21.573 --> 00:53:23.909
Even Aemond is all but vanquished.

593
00:53:24.910 --> 00:53:28.247
You will be queen
for many years after this.

594
00:53:29.248 --> 00:53:31.667
And your children's children after you.

595
00:53:36.839 --> 00:53:38.590
Just a little longer.

596
00:53:44.012 --> 00:53:45.222
Do you think...

597
00:53:46.640 --> 00:53:47.850
I am worthy?

598
00:53:50.519 --> 00:53:52.563
In this moment. my queen.

599
00:53:56.024 --> 00:53:57.526
Rhaenyra.

600
00:54:05.826 --> 00:54:08.162
I have never been more certain of it.

601
00:55:31.411 --> 00:55:34.081
A final stand then. Ser Tyland.

602
00:55:35.916 --> 00:55:37.292
Your Grace.

603
00:56:05.863 --> 00:56:10.409
We claim this land for Rhaenyra.
Queen of the Seven Kingdoms.

604
00:56:11.660 --> 00:56:13.888
You will throw down your arms

605
00:56:13.912 --> 00:56:16.206
and make ready to swear your fealty.

606
00:56:21.336 --> 00:56:23.046
No. no. no. no. no.

607
00:56:23.755 --> 00:56:24.756
Your Grace?

608
00:56:26.758 --> 00:56:28.135
Will you flee after all?

609
00:56:45.819 --> 00:56:48.530
We shall not surrender to the false queen.

610
00:56:56.830 --> 00:56:58.665
Is that you. Tyland Lannister?

611
00:56:59.958 --> 00:57:01.877
Your queen's been looking for you.

612
00:57:03.670 --> 00:57:05.940
Tell us where the gold is.

613
00:57:05.964 --> 00:57:09.009
and you will die
with your ears still attached.

614
00:57:22.648 --> 00:57:24.316
Behold me now!

615
00:57:26.777 --> 00:57:28.612
I am Aegon Targaryen!

616
00:57:30.364 --> 00:57:32.926
Viserys' true heir!

617
00:57:32.950 --> 00:57:36.638
The sixth King of the Andals
and the Rhoynar

618
00:57:36.662 --> 00:57:38.222
and the First Men!

619
00:57:38.246 --> 00:57:41.142
I was anointed by the High Septon

620
00:57:41.166 --> 00:57:43.102
in the light of the Seven.

621
00:57:43.126 --> 00:57:47.339
And it is in their light
that I stand before you now!

622
00:57:49.216 --> 00:57:51.569
Strike me down!

623
00:57:51.593 --> 00:57:54.763
And the Stranger will take retribution.

624
00:57:56.306 --> 00:57:59.810
The Warrior's sword
will be judgment upon you.

625
00:58:03.647 --> 00:58:04.647
Yes.

626
00:58:05.107 --> 00:58:06.400
Yes. cowards.

627
00:58:07.484 --> 00:58:09.319
You might well retreat.

628
00:58:10.028 --> 00:58:12.322
For now you see me as I truly am!

629
00:58:13.824 --> 00:58:16.135
Dreadful in vengeance!

630
00:58:16.159 --> 00:58:19.371
Righteous and glorious!

631
00:58:30.465 --> 00:58:31.842
Sunfyre.

632
00:58:39.141 --> 00:58:40.434
Sunfyre.

633
00:58:42.102 --> 00:58:43.645
<i>Dracarys.</i>

634
00:58:45.647 --> 00:58:48.066
Run! Save yourselves!

635
00:59:31.902 --> 00:59:33.236
Decent ale. that.

636
00:59:35.739 --> 00:59:37.282
I thought you might enjoy it.

637
00:59:43.538 --> 00:59:44.748
I have had word...

638
00:59:45.916 --> 00:59:49.169
since we last spoke
of a most distressing incident.

639
00:59:49.961 --> 00:59:53.173
My whisperers tell me that
Daemon Targaryen struck you.

640
00:59:54.341 --> 00:59:55.759
In the street.

641
00:59:57.969 --> 01:00:00.972
In front of all the commoners passing by.

642
01:00:02.140 --> 01:00:06.228
An intolerable insult
to someone of your stature.

643
01:00:08.188 --> 01:00:09.665
But then...

644
01:00:09.689 --> 01:00:12.502
it's almost to be
expected from those people.

645
01:00:12.526 --> 01:00:14.277
She did tell me not to go into town.

646
01:00:15.195 --> 01:00:17.048
- To be fair.
- Ludicrous.

647
01:00:17.072 --> 01:00:19.241
A man needs his sustenance and cheer.

648
01:00:21.368 --> 01:00:25.705
But it is obvious Rhaenyra and her ilk
regard you only as a tool.

649
01:00:27.707 --> 01:00:30.127
To be used and reprimanded.

650
01:00:32.587 --> 01:00:34.381
Whereas I understand...

651
01:00:35.882 --> 01:00:37.300
who you really are.

652
01:00:42.722 --> 01:00:45.058
You said last time...

653
01:00:47.185 --> 01:00:49.062
that you could give me a lordship.

654
01:00:51.231 --> 01:00:52.566
And a castle.

655
01:00:54.609 --> 01:00:55.694
Honeyholt.

656
01:00:57.529 --> 01:00:58.697
Honeyholt?

657
01:01:00.782 --> 01:01:02.409
Honeyholt is a trifle.

658
01:01:04.161 --> 01:01:08.623
It seems that Driftmark itself
may soon be without a master.

659
01:01:10.458 --> 01:01:12.627
Lord of the Tides.

660
01:01:14.629 --> 01:01:16.298
What do you think of that?

661
01:01:24.639 --> 01:01:26.474
They will laugh at you no more...

662
01:01:27.559 --> 01:01:29.269
when they see you as you are.

663
01:01:33.565 --> 01:01:34.733
No.

664
01:01:36.776 --> 01:01:38.111
They will burn.

665
01:01:39.305 --> 01:02:39.380
